#DESCRIPTION
Hybrid PIC (kinetic ions / fluid electrons) performance benchmark.  A Hall-term
whistler wave (the standard hybrid workload) on a 1D periodic grid sized to be a
representative scaling benchmark: 128 X cells, 2000 macroparticles/cell, so the
particle mover and the explicit Ohm's-law + Faraday field advance both dominate
the wall-clock.  This is the hybrid counterpart of performance/PARAM.in (the
full-PIC beam benchmark) and is exercised by tests/validate_performance.py.

Normalization matches the hybrid test family (hybrid_whistler): lNormSI ~ d_i,
uNormSI ~ v_A so d_i ~ v_A ~ 1 and (for the proton) B ~ Omega_i ~ 1 in code
units.  The Hall/whistler mode is sub-cycled (nHallSubcycle = 8) so the explicit
advance stays RK4-stable at dt = 0.02; this exercises the sub-cycling machinery
that dominates the hybrid field-solver cost.

#INITFROMSWMF
F                       initFromSWMF

#GEOMETRY
-3.2                    xMin  [code units; Lx = 6.4 d_i]
 3.2                    xMax
-0.05                   yMin
 0.05                   yMax
-0.05                   zMin
 0.05                   zMax

#NCELL
128                     nCellX
1                       nCellY
1                       nCellZ

#MAXBLOCKSIZE
64                      maxBlockSizeX
1                       maxBlockSizeY
1                       maxBlockSizeZ

#PERIODICITY
T                       isPeriodicX
T                       isPeriodicY
T                       isPeriodicZ

Standard Maxwell/GMRES solver disabled; use the Ohm's-law + Faraday hybrid
field advance instead.
#SOLVEEM
F                       solveEM

#HYBRIDPIC
T                       useHybridPIC

#AVGFIELDB
T                       useAvgFieldB
20                      nAvgFieldB

Hall-only: resistive and electron-pressure-gradient terms are turned off
(both 0.0) to isolate the whistler dispersion (the standard hybrid workload).
#RESISTIVITY
0.0                     etaResistivity  [m^2/s, SI magnetic diffusivity]

#ELECTRONTEMPERATURE
0.0                     electronTemperature  [eV]
1.0                     electronGamma
1.0                     electronDensity0

Sub-cycle the B update: the explicit Hall advance is limited by the discrete
grid-scale whistler mode.  nHallSubcycle = 8 exercises the sub-cycling machinery
(4x cheaper than 32 while still exercising it).
#HALLSUBCYCLE
8                       nHallSubcycle

Single kinetic ion species (q = m = 1); the electron is an implicit
neutralizing massless fluid, so no electron particle species is present.
#PLASMA
1                       nSpecies
1.0                     mass
1.0                     charge

#UNIFORMSTATE
5.0                     rho [amu/cc]   Species 0: ions (n = 5 /cc)
0.0                     ux [km/s]
0.0                     uy [km/s]
0.0                     uz [km/s]
10000.0                 T [K]
5.2195e-9               bx [T]       uniform guide field Bx0 (B_code ~ 1)
0.0                     by [T]
0.0                     bz [T]
0.0                     ex [V/m]
0.0                     ey [V/m]
0.0                     ez [V/m]

#TESTCASE
HybridWave

#TIMESTEPPING
T                       useFixedDt
0.02                    dt

#NORMALIZATION
1.0e5                   lNormSI   [m]  ~ d_i so d_i ~ 1 in code units
5.0e4                   uNormSI   [m/s] ~ v_A so v_A ~ 1 in code units

#MONITOR
50                      dnReport

#SAVELOG
100                     dnSavePic
100                     dnSavePT

#PARTICLES
2000                    nParticle per cell in X
1                       nParticle per cell in Y
1                       nParticle per cell in Z

#COMOVING
F                       solvePartInCoMov
0                       nSmoothBackGroundU

#UPWINDE
F                       useUpwindE
0.0                     limiterThetaE

#UPWINDB
F                       doSmoothB
0.0                     theta

#SAVEPLOT
0                                 nPlot

#STOP
-1                      MaxIter
1.0                     TimeMax

#RUN
